 ],
 "note": "3-door Sierra RS500 body (with the RS500 rear wing) confirmed by every BBC graphics drawing and all photos, so the 2.0 non-turbo car used the RS500 shell, not the Sapphire. Measured on Super Touring Register 4708 (right side, side-on, mirrored to our side; x scaled between the wheel centres, y as a share of the beltline-to-door-bottom height, bumper stickers by the front wheel centre); left-side order of the door stickers (Raychem, personal, Willans) and the window name from Super Touring Register 4709 (left side, 3/4 front). ESSO board on the front door, ANDY MIDDLEHURST small on the wing, Champion and Yokohama on the bumpers, demon tweeks windscreen band from the TV frames. Wheels: gold BBS cross-spoke with polished lip, from the on-track photos (no standing photo found). This is the summer livery; the round 15 TV frame shows GRAHAM GOODE RACING in black along the doors, a later change not drawn here. Uncertain: windscreen band shape (seen from the front only), sticker logos simplified."
